-- W67 (O12, M14): `&&` and `||` chains of 200 operands, twice the length that
-- exceeded the host parser's nesting (~100). Both are right-associative
-- and short-circuit: the chain is cut into bindings that are forced only
-- when the operator before them did not decide, so an `error` operand
-- past the deciding one is never evaluated, exactly as GHC. Pinned
-- against GHC at the first, a middle, the last and a non-deciding operand,
-- with a raising operand after the chain and operands that are calls.

